  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"we should be able to set start points on generated path and also exit points.. So the path gets regenerated to those.\"\n\nWhat is missing: where an operation starts cutting and where it leaves is chosen by the generator alone. The user cannot say \"enter here\" or \"leave here\", for example to keep the entry mark off a visible face, to start a contour away from a clamp, or to end next to the following feature.\n\nWanted: on the operations where it has a meaning (2D Contour, Pocket, Adaptive, Face, Slot, Bore, and the 3D finishing passes that have a free start), two optional picks:\n- Start point(s): picked in the viewport (a point on the model, a sketch point or typed coordinates). For a closed contour the path is re-sequenced to begin at the pick's nearest point on the chain, with its lead-in there; for a pocket or adaptive region the entry (helix, ramp or plunge) is placed at the pick. One pick per chain or region; chains with no pick keep the automatic choice.\n- Exit point(s): the same for where the pass ends and the lead-out is placed.\n\nChanging a pick is an undoable command (it edits the operation parameters) and regenerates the path. MCP: the same parameters on the operation tools.\n\nSafety: a pick is a wish, never an override of a check. If the entry, lead or ramp at the picked place does not fit (helix does not fit in the region, lead-in gouges a wall, the point is outside the machinable region or inside a keep-out or fixture), the operation is refused by name or marked incomplete, saying which pick and why; it never moves the entry silently and never posts a path that the collision or gouge checks would refuse at the automatic entry.\n\nRelated: the companion issue on pre-drilled holes as entry positions (filed with this one).\n\nDone means: a closed 2D contour with a picked start begins and leads in at that point and, with a picked exit, leads out there (golden CL); a pocket enters at its picked point; an impossible pick is refused by name in a test; undo and redo restore the previous path; the MCP tools take the picks; the structural UI test covers the two pick rows.\n",
